          <p>
            The generators here are conventional units: the engine runs at a fixed 3,600 rpm and output quality depends on holding that speed. That makes them loud — 68 to 76 dB under load — and gives them total harmonic distortion in the 15-25% range, which is fine for motors, heaters, and lights but is not ideal for laptops and modern electronics without a surge protector or line conditioner in between. What you get in exchange is roughly double the watts per dollar of an inverter unit, which is why this category exists.
