            Do not pick a fuel — use both deliberately. Keep three or four propane tanks as the strategic reserve, since they never go stale. Use gasoline when you need maximum output or when it is genuinely cold. And run the generator on propane for its monthly exercise runs, because propane leaves no varnish, so the carburetor stays clean in a machine that spends most of its life sitting still.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-2xl p-6 my-8">
